The ruling file is at `/Users/mindlace/Projects/sfhousing/.claude/worktrees/incremental-game/.superpowers/superconductor/incremental-game/rulings/game-shell-1.md`.

**Ruling (the question's option A):** whether Paint is won now depends only on the latest complete score. A score that is not yet complete (during a stroke, or while the worker is still filling) leaves the won state alone. So after "Keep playing", the card stays closed and the level cell's "Level up" doesn't flicker during a stroke that keeps the room at or above the goal. Paint stops being won only when a complete score falls below the goal. At that point the offer is cleared, and a later complete score that crosses the goal again reopens the card.

- **Commit:** `0b187d7c`. It amends the game-shell spec's "Paint's win" section and adds one test case to `page.game.svelte.spec.ts`: after "Keep playing", a stroke leaves the card closed and the offer set the whole time.
- **Interfaces:** no interface row or contracts code changed.
- **Affected unit:** game-shell. Its plan's Task 4 (Paint's win) was written on the literal reading the question describes, so it no longer holds and its branch is cut back to before that task.
